    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The only test class (`AcceptanceTest`, which includes the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` checkpoint) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern, mirroring how `namesakeCount` already works.\n\n**Logic** (`Owner.getMembershipTier()`): GOLD now takes precedence when the owner's household has 3+ members as of creation; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter, and updated the transient `getMembershipTier()` to return `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, falling back to the prior SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n- **`rest/function/owner/CountHousehold.java`** (new step) \u2014 after `AssignHousehold` has set the new owner's `householdId` and back-filled existing members, it counts existing owners sharing that `householdId` and adds one for the owner being created (not yet saved); a solo owner gets size 1.\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `countHousehold` into the pipeline between `assignHousehold` and `countNamesakes` (under the same `transaction` governance).\n- **Schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe counting step runs after household back-fill but before `SaveOwner`, so for the test's third shared-household member it sees 2 existing members + 1 (itself) = 3 \u2192 GOLD, which is read back correctly via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
